  <h2>Research Interests</h2>
  <p>
    I am interested in mathematical and statistical methodology for spatially structured
    biomedical data, especially histopathology images and related imaging-derived
    measurements. My current interests include spatial statistics, topological data
    analysis, and computational methods for biologically meaningful problems.
  </p>

  <h2>Projects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://lce.biohpc.swmed.edu/sashimi/">SASHIMI</a>. A framework for spatial
      analysis of AI-segmented histopathology images, with emphasis on marked point pattern
      data and interpretable spatial summaries.
    </li>
    <li>
      Topological summaries of tumor architecture. Placeholder for future project description
